think r1 (crux) · r2 (travels) · r3 (across a Knot) landed and pushed both remotes. The closing rung carries the reader onto a REAL on-disk Cord record carrying a genuine reverting chain a keeper can open and walk, proving the Braid's signature property — atomic all-or-nothing — is true to the bytes. Mirrored pledge_true/purse_true: a fixture generator, an @embedFile app reporting a triple, an independent awk cross-check, all wired by the r4 witness.
think Chose a REVERTING chain (not committing) for the fixture because it uniquely exercises the Braid's crux — a chain whose final link overdraws reverses whole, moving not one coin. Genesis Alice 100 · Bob 50; braid routes Alice→Bob 100, Bob→Carol 120, Carol→Dave 200; Carol holds only the 120 link 1 routed to her, so the final link overdraws and the whole atom rejects. The app reports (terminal-recipient-hex=Dave, committed 0, rejected 1) and asserts the terminal recipient received nothing and balances stand as genesis left them.
think The awk does GENUINE balance simulation (not just structural tallying) — it seeds each account's balance from the kind-1 genesis credits (body=recipient hex, amount=$5), gathers each braid's links by id and seq (body $7 = 4c·id·seq·last·to, signer $8 = from, amount $5), and when a chain closes SIMULATES it atomically over a fresh delta scratch: each sender must afford reading its balance forward through the chain's own earlier moves; all afford → commit, any cannot → reject. Honest on this fixture because genesis is first and the chain is round-ascending, so file order equals the agreed order. Used split("",d) to clear the scratch portably and a hand-rolled hexval (no gawk strtonum dependency).
obs GREEN first pass on selftest. app measure and awk both print `ed3234b2… 0 1` (Dave's terminal · committed 0 · rejected 1) — two tools, one answer, byte-identical. One gotcha proven-and-handled: the app's hosted print writes to STDERR (std.debug.print), so the measure triple is captured with 2>&1 (as pledge_true's witness already does) — the fixture generator likewise emits on stderr. The fixture is reproducible (the generator re-emits byte-identical bytes, diff -q clean). A tampered header refuses BadFormat. Conservation (balances_sum == total_issued == 150) holds over the real bytes. TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, both new .rye files no findings.
